# Deny direct access to repo-internal paths that must never be served.
# robots.txt only asks crawlers not to index these — it does nothing to stop
# a direct request, a scraper, or a git-history-dumping tool. This file is
# the actual access control, honored natively by Netlify and Cloudflare
# Pages (same hosts _headers already targets — see that file).
#
# This is a safety net, not the real fix: the most reliable protection is to
# simply never publish .git/, scripts/, or supabase/ in the deployed folder
# at all. If your host lets you set a separate "publish directory" or
# ignore list, use that instead of relying on these rules alone.

/.git/*       /404.html   404
/.git         /404.html   404
/scripts/*    /404.html   404
/supabase/*   /404.html   404
